abstract: >-
  A paper and release repository proving that the explicit positive compact
  kernel K on the squarefree integers, the limit of normalized Gram matrices
  of the inverses of sparse Mertens matrices, has eigenvalues
  lambda_r(K) ~ (6/pi^2)/(r log r), with the corresponding counting and
  cumulative laws, and that the same laws hold for its rank-one deflation.
  The proof uses a cylinder Gram representation, a tree interlacing
  sandwich, and classical smooth-number estimates. No convergence rate and
  no estimate for the Mertens function are claimed.
keywords:
